---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data, including the analytics service we use.`} updated="2026-11-05">
  <p>This policy explains what happens to your data when you visit {SITE.name}. The short version: we don't run accounts, newsletters or comments on this site, and we don't set cookies ourselves. We do use GoatCounter, a third-party analytics service, to count visits.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We don't ask you for personal information. There are no sign-ups or forms on this site. The technical data described under Hosting, Analytics and YouTube videos below is handled when you visit.</p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is a set of static pages served by our hosting provider (currently GitHub Pages). Like any web server, the host may log technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, to keep the service secure and running. That processing is governed by the host's own privacy policy, for example the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" rel="noopener">GoatCounter</a>, a third-party analytics service, to see how many visits the site gets and which pages people read. A small script, loaded from gc.zgo.at, runs on every page and sends GoatCounter a record of the page view.</p>
  <p>According to GoatCounter's documentation, it uses that record to keep aggregate counts of:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the page's address and title</li>
    <li>the page or site that referred you, including any campaign tags in the link</li>
    <li>your browser and operating system, worked out from headers your browser sends (for example, Firefox 139 and Windows 11)</li>
    <li>your screen size</li>
    <li>your approximate location (your country, and your region in some countries), worked out from your IP address</li>
  </ul>
  <p>GoatCounter says these are stored as separate counts per hour or day, with no way to link them to each other. It says it doesn't store your IP address, the full User-Agent header or any tracker ID, and that it doesn't store any information in your browser with cookies, local storage, cache or any other method. To recognize repeat visits, it keeps the site name, your IP address and your User-Agent in memory only, for up to eight hours.</p>
  <p>GoatCounter says no information is shared with third parties, and that data is stored on servers at Hetzner Online GmbH in Finland and Germany. The counts stay in our GoatCounter account until we delete them. If your browser sends a Do Not Track signal, we've set the script not to count your visit. For more, see the <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy" rel="noopener">GoatCounter privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
  <p>Posts include a preview image of the related YouTube video. The preview image is loaded from YouTube's image servers (i.ytimg.com), which can see your IP address, as with any web request. The actual video player is <strong>not</strong> loaded until you click play. When you do, the player loads from YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain (youtube-nocookie.com), and YouTube may then collect data under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Your settings</h2>
  <p>If you use the light/dark switch, your choice is saved in your own browser's local storage so the site remembers it. It never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time by clearing your browser's site data.</p>

  <h2>Future changes</h2>
  <p>If we ever add advertising, affiliate links or a different analytics service, some of those services may use cookies or similar technology. We'll update this page before that happens and change the date above. Affiliate links will always be disclosed; see our <a href={href('affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is a general-audience site and isn't directed at children under 13. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? See our <a href={href('contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
